00:00:09.413 --> 00:00:10.395
Baby number three, right?

00:00:10.395 --> 00:00:11.499
Is on the way?
- Yes, yes.

00:00:11.499 --> 00:00:14.242
- That's so exciting.
(audience cheering)

00:00:14.242 --> 00:00:17.305
Are you excited or worried
about being outnumbered or--

00:00:17.305 --> 00:00:18.242
- It's like sometimes you just

00:00:18.242 --> 00:00:20.462
make poor life choices and
you gotta roll with them.

00:00:20.462 --> 00:00:21.295
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:21.295 --> 00:00:22.275
- And you roll up your sleeves.

00:00:22.275 --> 00:00:23.583
- We're insane, we're insane.
- Yeah.

00:00:23.583 --> 00:00:25.058
- Can I just show you
something real quick?

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:27.134
- Yes.
- Before we continue,

00:00:27.134 --> 00:00:28.479
'cause I'm super proud of it.

00:00:28.479 --> 00:00:30.674
- Okay.
- Look at this right here.

00:00:30.674 --> 00:00:33.674
(audience cheering)

00:00:37.289 --> 00:00:40.082
- Is it two thousand--
- I did that.

00:00:40.082 --> 00:00:41.177
- [Kelly] Oh my god.

00:00:41.177 --> 00:00:42.182
- Me and eBay.

00:00:42.182 --> 00:00:43.762
- Oh my god, I love you and eBay.

00:00:43.762 --> 00:00:44.949
- Yeah.
- Oh god.

00:00:44.949 --> 00:00:47.637
- It's a women's medium, so it's tight.

00:00:47.637 --> 00:00:48.537
- I love it.

00:00:48.537 --> 00:00:49.370
I love it.

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:50.613
It'd be snug on me too, brother.

00:00:50.613 --> 00:00:53.794
So how did your wife like, let you know?

00:00:53.794 --> 00:00:57.405
- Okay, so it was
actually a beautiful day.

00:00:57.405 --> 00:01:00.396
Like, I'm eight years sober,

00:01:00.396 --> 00:01:02.591
so it was like my sober birthday

00:01:02.591 --> 00:01:03.564
and she wrote me a card

00:01:03.564 --> 00:01:05.449
and it was to say congratulations.

00:01:05.449 --> 00:01:06.282
And she was like--

00:01:06.282 --> 00:01:08.255
- First of all, eight years sober.

00:01:08.255 --> 00:01:09.088
(clapping)

00:01:09.088 --> 00:01:09.921
Yeah.

00:01:09.921 --> 00:01:11.948
- I did it all by myself.
- That's incredible.

00:01:11.948 --> 00:01:13.845
- No help.
- No help at all.

00:01:13.845 --> 00:01:14.895
- Nope. Came in on a winning streak.

00:01:14.895 --> 00:01:15.728
- No support.

00:01:15.728 --> 00:01:16.561
- Yep.

00:01:16.561 --> 00:01:18.508
It's been a joyful
journey the entire time.

00:01:18.508 --> 00:01:19.573
- That's awesome, though.

00:01:19.573 --> 00:01:20.821
- So she said, "congrats"

00:01:20.821 --> 00:01:22.492
and she said, "just so you know,

00:01:22.492 --> 00:01:24.639
on your ninth sober anniversary,

00:01:24.639 --> 00:01:26.629
you're gonna be a father of three".

00:01:26.629 --> 00:01:29.269
And so it was this like
wonderful little revelation

00:01:29.269 --> 00:01:30.172
and I was like, I knew it.

00:01:30.172 --> 00:01:31.621
You've been acting weird all week.

00:01:31.621 --> 00:01:32.860
I knew you were pregnant.

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:34.252
- Women love to hear that.

00:01:34.252 --> 00:01:35.330
- Yeah. You've been strange.

00:01:35.330 --> 00:01:36.434
- I thought you were moody.

00:01:36.434 --> 00:01:39.175
- You've been unusually kind all week.

00:01:39.175 --> 00:01:42.126
No.
- She went the other way.

00:01:42.126 --> 00:01:44.377
- And then we went to a Diwali party

00:01:44.377 --> 00:01:46.537
that night at the White House.

00:01:46.537 --> 00:01:47.370
- That's awesome.

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:49.033
- Which I'd never been to the White House.

00:01:49.033 --> 00:01:49.945
It was incredible.

00:01:49.945 --> 00:01:52.128
We dressed up, we got all gussied up.

00:01:52.128 --> 00:01:55.311
They took us through like
four things of security

00:01:55.311 --> 00:01:57.759
and it's a Diwali party,
which is Indian New Year.

00:01:57.759 --> 00:01:58.885
It's how we celebrate.

00:01:58.885 --> 00:02:00.313
- Beautiful.
- Yeah.

00:02:00.313 --> 00:02:02.533
Now, Indians like to eat food.

00:02:02.533 --> 00:02:04.658
We enjoy eating on Diwali.

00:02:04.658 --> 00:02:06.217
- So do Southerners.
- Yeah.

00:02:06.217 --> 00:02:08.799
- Just every day, not just like the one.

00:02:08.799 --> 00:02:10.562
- Lot of comparisons.
- Yeah.

00:02:10.562 --> 00:02:12.252
- Between Texans and Indians.

00:02:12.252 --> 00:02:13.129
Yeah.
- Totally.

00:02:13.129 --> 00:02:16.018
- Very fine line separating us.

00:02:16.018 --> 00:02:17.663
But we get to this Diwali party

00:02:17.663 --> 00:02:19.376
and Mr. President speaks

00:02:19.376 --> 00:02:23.388
and Kamala Harris speaks
and Jill, president--

00:02:23.388 --> 00:02:24.540
- Biden?
- Yes. Jill Biden.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:26.687
- Doctor--
- Doctor Biden. Yes. Oof.

00:02:26.687 --> 00:02:27.954
- Got a lot of titles.

00:02:27.954 --> 00:02:29.250
- Yeah, well I should've figured out

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:30.668
what to call 'em before
I sat on this couch.

00:02:30.668 --> 00:02:31.809
- [Kelly] I know.

00:02:31.809 --> 00:02:33.535
- But there was no food at this party.

00:02:33.535 --> 00:02:34.743
- What?
- None.

00:02:34.743 --> 00:02:36.245
There were like hors
d'oeuvre, finger food.

00:02:36.245 --> 00:02:37.078
So my wife--

00:02:37.078 --> 00:02:38.009
- Was it because of
like Covid or something?

00:02:38.009 --> 00:02:38.842
- I don't know.

00:02:38.842 --> 00:02:39.907
I just think they don't know Indian people

00:02:39.907 --> 00:02:41.177
as well as they should at this point.

00:02:41.177 --> 00:02:42.720
- Oh, okay, okay.

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:43.553
- But my wife and I,

00:02:43.553 --> 00:02:45.871
luckily my mom and dad
live right outside of DC.

00:02:45.871 --> 00:02:48.340
They're about 25 minutes
from the White House.

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:51.079
So we came, we saw them
speak, we got dressed up,

00:02:51.079 --> 00:02:53.663
we took some pictures and
then we went straight home

00:02:53.663 --> 00:02:55.572
and had a full feast at
home with the family.

00:02:55.572 --> 00:02:57.245
- Yes. You did it right.
- On Diwali.

00:02:57.245 --> 00:02:58.078
Yeah, exactly.

00:02:58.078 --> 00:02:59.353
I was like, mom, you gotta do it up.

00:02:59.353 --> 00:03:00.613
Let's go.
- Yeah.

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:02.387
- So we had a formal dinner at home,

00:03:02.387 --> 00:03:03.259
which was really nice.

00:03:03.259 --> 00:03:04.300
- I like that.

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:05.507
Do you get home often?

00:03:05.507 --> 00:03:06.924
Do you get back home?

00:03:06.924 --> 00:03:08.773
- No, not really as much as I should.

00:03:08.773 --> 00:03:09.941
- That's why's special though,

00:03:09.941 --> 00:03:11.669
that you were in town
and you got to do that.

00:03:11.669 --> 00:03:12.502
That's cool.

00:03:12.502 --> 00:03:14.142
- Yeah, my parents love to have me home

00:03:14.142 --> 00:03:15.234
and tell me to stay there.

00:03:15.234 --> 00:03:16.067
My mom's like,

00:03:16.067 --> 00:03:17.113
"There's a room in the basement,

00:03:17.113 --> 00:03:18.385
you could just come back in".
(laughs)

00:03:18.385 --> 00:03:20.160
- And you can be that guy
living in your mom's basement.

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:21.545
- She's like, "look, this acting thing,

00:03:21.545 --> 00:03:25.180
let's be honest, it's not
really working out for you.

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:28.727
You should have been a doctor,
at the very least a PhD".

00:03:28.727 --> 00:03:30.164
- Oh my God.

00:03:30.164 --> 00:03:31.267
- "Just come to the basement,

00:03:31.267 --> 00:03:32.821
there's an en suite bathroom.

00:03:32.821 --> 00:03:34.039
You have everything you need".

00:03:34.039 --> 00:03:35.153
- You don't wanna be that guy.

00:03:35.153 --> 00:03:36.635
Well, speaking of family,

00:03:36.635 --> 00:03:39.576
we saw online that y'all
got Guinea pigs recently.

00:03:39.576 --> 00:03:41.685
Did you get your kids?
(audience gasps)

00:03:41.685 --> 00:03:45.108
Oh my God, your dog gets
along with your Guinea pig?

00:03:45.108 --> 00:03:48.835
My dog tried to eat our Guinea
pig when we were little.

00:03:48.835 --> 00:03:50.166
- My dog--
- It's traumatic.

00:03:50.166 --> 00:03:54.450
- My dog likes to eat
other animal's feces,

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:56.216
so she likes to hang out around.

00:03:56.216 --> 00:03:57.496
- That's a dog thing.

00:03:57.496 --> 00:03:58.860
- Yo. When we had the cat,

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:00.529
she was all up in the kitty litter box.

00:04:00.529 --> 00:04:01.362
- Yeah.

00:04:01.362 --> 00:04:02.233
- And now with the Guinea pigs,

00:04:02.233 --> 00:04:04.972
she's just straight up
like mouth to the butt.

00:04:04.972 --> 00:04:06.736
Just--
(audience chattering)

00:04:06.736 --> 00:04:07.724
Like a feeder.

00:04:07.724 --> 00:04:09.449
Yeah. Yeah.

00:04:09.449 --> 00:04:11.087
It's gross.
- Like a feeder.

00:04:11.087 --> 00:04:12.356
- But you know, I love Guinea pigs.

00:04:12.356 --> 00:04:13.752
My wife wasn't sure about it.

00:04:13.752 --> 00:04:16.566
And what happened was,
my mom, she works at NIH,

00:04:16.566 --> 00:04:18.929
National Institutes of
Health in Bethesda, Maryland.

00:04:18.929 --> 00:04:21.322
And at the time, this
was like 25 years ago,

00:04:21.322 --> 00:04:24.620
they used to do animal experiments.

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:27.570
Like they used to dissect
rats and things like that.

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:31.812
And once upon a time they got
this Guinea pig in the lab

00:04:31.812 --> 00:04:33.251
and everyone fell in love with it.

00:04:33.251 --> 00:04:34.439
And I showed up and I was like,

00:04:34.439 --> 00:04:37.186
"Mom, you can't, please don't
cut this Guinea pig open.

00:04:37.186 --> 00:04:38.891
I love this Guinea pig".
- Oh my God. That's traumatic.

00:04:38.891 --> 00:04:40.210
- Yeah. I was like, "Please".

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:42.963
And my mother, being the
sweet woman that she is,

00:04:42.963 --> 00:04:44.643
stole the Guinea pig from NIH.

00:04:44.643 --> 00:04:45.589
(laughs)

00:04:45.589 --> 00:04:48.613
She smuggled that (beep)
out in a cardboard box

00:04:48.613 --> 00:04:52.088
and picked me up from school
one day and there she was.

00:04:52.088 --> 00:04:54.597
And that Guinea pig
lived with us for years,

00:04:54.597 --> 00:04:56.425
probably several, you know,

00:04:56.425 --> 00:04:57.926
medical issues and things like that.

00:04:57.926 --> 00:04:59.007
But--
- Yeah.

00:04:59.007 --> 00:05:02.072
- She was there with us for
like four or five years.

00:05:02.072 --> 00:05:04.489
So when Tiare, my daughter,
said she wanted Guinea pigs

00:05:04.489 --> 00:05:05.629
I was like, we gotta do it.

00:05:05.629 --> 00:05:06.462
- So stoked.

00:05:06.462 --> 00:05:07.732
- They're a huge part of my childhood.

00:05:07.732 --> 00:05:10.147
Emancipating one from
a government facility?

00:05:10.147 --> 00:05:11.114
- This is a movie.

00:05:11.114 --> 00:05:12.772
- Yeah. Statue of limitations is over,

00:05:12.772 --> 00:05:14.167
so, y'all can't do (beep).

00:05:14.167 --> 00:05:16.521
Sorry. You can't do anything to my mother.

00:05:16.521 --> 00:05:17.792
- Speaking of like the White House,

00:05:17.792 --> 00:05:18.966
you brought that up a moment ago

00:05:18.966 --> 00:05:20.637
and I was like, when I
went to the White House

00:05:20.637 --> 00:05:21.897
I thought the crazy thing was

00:05:21.897 --> 00:05:24.218
there's all this security
to get in, right?

00:05:24.218 --> 00:05:25.929
But then once you're in,

00:05:25.929 --> 00:05:29.572
literally me and my ex like walked around

00:05:29.572 --> 00:05:32.323
and we were like, "I
guess we can do this".

00:05:32.323 --> 00:05:33.394
Like, we just--

00:05:33.394 --> 00:05:34.802
I mean, I'm sure there's
cameras everywhere, obviously,

00:05:34.802 --> 00:05:37.753
but we just walked around.

00:05:37.753 --> 00:05:40.441
- I stole so--
(laughing)

00:05:40.441 --> 00:05:43.076
So many napkins, first of all.

00:05:43.076 --> 00:05:45.008
- I didn't steal, but I left something.

00:05:45.008 --> 00:05:45.841
- What'd you leave?

00:05:45.841 --> 00:05:47.192
- I think it was jade.

00:05:47.192 --> 00:05:49.480
It was like, one of the times I went,

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:51.699
I think I left a green
piece of like, jade.

00:05:51.699 --> 00:05:52.569
For good luck.

00:05:52.569 --> 00:05:53.402
- So cool.

00:05:53.402 --> 00:05:54.235
- Just for, yeah.

00:05:54.235 --> 00:05:55.068
We need it, right? Like, yeah.

00:05:55.068 --> 00:05:55.901
- We think differently.

00:05:55.901 --> 00:05:57.339
'Cause I was trying to steal some books.

00:05:57.339 --> 00:05:59.438
- Dude, I was like, jade, sage,

00:05:59.438 --> 00:06:01.559
I was all the things I was trying to do.

00:06:01.559 --> 00:06:04.933
- They have the presidential
china just sitting on a wall.

00:06:04.933 --> 00:06:06.107
I'm not gonna take a tea cup?

00:06:06.107 --> 00:06:07.118
What? Like, come on

00:06:07.118 --> 00:06:07.951
(audience laughing)

00:06:07.951 --> 00:06:08.784
What are we doing here?

00:06:08.784 --> 00:06:09.617
- What are we doing?

00:06:09.617 --> 00:06:10.489
I definitely would've done that.

00:06:10.489 --> 00:06:11.322
I feel like--

00:06:11.322 --> 00:06:12.880
Yeah, people would've come
down from the ceiling--

00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:14.769
- Swarm, swarm. Yeah.
- or something.

00:06:14.769 --> 00:06:16.187
But first let's talk about your kids.

00:06:16.187 --> 00:06:17.491
You have a three year old, right?

00:06:17.491 --> 00:06:18.348
Is he potty trained yet?

00:06:18.348 --> 00:06:19.305
Or are you still going through it?

00:06:19.305 --> 00:06:20.179
- How old is your son?

00:06:20.179 --> 00:06:21.626
- My son's six, we're about to be seven.

00:06:21.626 --> 00:06:23.085
And my daughter's about to be nine.

00:06:23.085 --> 00:06:24.146
- He--

00:06:24.146 --> 00:06:25.177
- Look at that sweater.

00:06:25.177 --> 00:06:26.067
- Yeah.
- Style.

00:06:26.067 --> 00:06:27.811
- My wife knows how to do it for sure.

00:06:27.811 --> 00:06:28.747
- Yeah.

00:06:28.747 --> 00:06:31.214
- We're trying to potty train him.

00:06:31.214 --> 00:06:33.006
Like, we incentivized by giving him

00:06:33.006 --> 00:06:35.856
like Hot Wheels cars
if he uses the toilet.

00:06:35.856 --> 00:06:38.533
So he's got like a hundred Hot Wheels cars

00:06:38.533 --> 00:06:43.257
and is still dropping like
adult size grenades in diapers.

00:06:43.257 --> 00:06:44.181
- Yeah.

00:06:44.181 --> 00:06:45.943
- He's very much against that potty.

00:06:45.943 --> 00:06:46.776
He's all about--

00:06:46.776 --> 00:06:49.230
- It's amazing to how little
they are and what comes out.

00:06:49.230 --> 00:06:50.691
- It's astounding.

00:06:50.691 --> 00:06:52.077
- It's incredible.

00:06:52.077 --> 00:06:54.041
- It's a war crime.

00:06:54.041 --> 00:06:55.994
It's really, really, it's messed up.

00:06:55.994 --> 00:06:56.827
- [Kelly] I know.

00:06:56.827 --> 00:06:58.063
- And then he'll ask me to hold his hands

00:06:58.063 --> 00:06:58.896
and he'll be like,
- No.

00:06:58.896 --> 00:06:59.799
- "Breathe with me.

00:06:59.799 --> 00:07:01.803
Papa. Papa, Papa.

00:07:01.803 --> 00:07:02.708
Breathe with me".

00:07:02.708 --> 00:07:05.236
- My daughter used to do that.

00:07:05.236 --> 00:07:07.236
- "Can you go get mama?"

00:07:09.341 --> 00:07:11.032
- My daughter used to be like,
"Can you hold my hands?".

00:07:11.032 --> 00:07:12.910
And then she (chuckles).

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:14.884
I don't think we need to be here for this.

00:07:14.884 --> 00:07:15.748
- I know, right?

00:07:15.748 --> 00:07:16.966
We have to like--

00:07:16.966 --> 00:07:18.100
Can you blink?

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:18.933
- [Kelly] Private time.

00:07:18.933 --> 00:07:19.766
- Do we have to stare so deeply

00:07:19.766 --> 00:07:21.701
into each other's eyes right now?

00:07:21.701 --> 00:07:23.800
The only good thing is
only my wife is allowed

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:24.893
to clean the dookies.

00:07:24.893 --> 00:07:25.775
Like I'm not allowed to.

00:07:25.775 --> 00:07:26.608
- Oh, they won't let--

00:07:26.608 --> 00:07:28.770
- So I'll be like,
well, you don't want me.

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:30.671
Sorry. No gagging for me today.

00:07:30.671 --> 00:07:32.748
- Yeah. It's a crazy thing being a parent.

00:07:32.748 --> 00:07:34.638
Okay. Here is a photo of your daughter.

00:07:34.638 --> 00:07:35.772
She's eight, right?

00:07:35.772 --> 00:07:38.578
- She's gonna be eight in a week. Yeah.

00:07:38.578 --> 00:07:40.047
- She is fabulous

00:07:40.047 --> 00:07:42.881
and very Janice Joplin
vibes right now going on.

00:07:42.881 --> 00:07:43.869
I like it

00:07:43.869 --> 00:07:45.046
- That's her at Comic Con.

00:07:45.046 --> 00:07:47.972
Dressed like Sheila Carrasco
who plays Flower in "Ghosts".

00:07:47.972 --> 00:07:48.805
- [Kelly] Oh, yeah.

00:07:48.805 --> 00:07:49.855
- That's her in cosplay.

00:07:49.855 --> 00:07:50.821
- Oh, that's awesome.

00:07:50.821 --> 00:07:52.127
- Yeah. Although she would dress like

00:07:52.127 --> 00:07:53.440
that on a daily basis, anyways.

00:07:53.440 --> 00:07:54.552
- My daughter loves dress up as well.

00:07:54.552 --> 00:07:55.422
- She'd be stoked.

00:07:55.422 --> 00:07:56.408
- So does my son.

00:07:56.408 --> 00:07:57.857
Well, everyone loves "Ghosts".

00:07:57.857 --> 00:07:58.690
Congratulations.

00:07:58.690 --> 00:07:59.523
- Thank you.

00:07:59.523 --> 00:08:00.378
- Such a success.

00:08:00.378 --> 00:08:03.120
So tell your mom you
didn't need to be a doctor.

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:04.202
- She would disagree with you.

00:08:04.202 --> 00:08:05.587
You should take that out.
(Kelly laughs)

00:08:05.587 --> 00:08:08.347
That's not gonna go over well with my mom.

00:08:08.347 --> 00:08:10.742
- So wait, tell us what's
